===Noun===
[[File:Musician - The Noun Project.svg|thumb|150px|A musician playing a {{l|en|guitar}}]]
{{en-noun}}

# A [[composer]], [[conductor]], or [[performer]] of [[music]]; specifically, a person who sings and/or plays a [[musical instrument]] as a [[hobby]], [[occupation]], or [[profession]].
#: {{ux|en|Jenny is a talented '''musician''', playing the cello, saxophone, piano and guitar.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=27-06-2024|author=Clay Risen|title=Kinky Friedman, 79, Dies; '''Musician''' and Humorist Slew Sacred Cows|work=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/06/27/arts/music/kinky-friedman-dead.html|passage=He joined Little Jewford and other '''musicians''' — all with outlandish stage names, like Wichita Culpepper and Sky Cap Adams — to form Kinky Friedman and the Texas Jewboys in 1973.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=05-09-2024|author=Maia Coleman|title=The Bands and the Fans Were Fake. The $10 Million Was Real.|work=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/09/05/nyregion/nc-man-charged-ai-fake-music.html|passage=Mr. Smith, a flesh-and-blood '''musician''', produced A.I.-generated music and played it billions of times using bots he had programmed, according to the indictment.}}

